# Phase 18 compatibility release gate — execution log

- P18-V01 follow-up: the pinned Java `MessageAccessor.cloneMessage` helper was
  covered through Producer selector preparation but had no direct Rust public
  API mapping. Added `Message::clone_message`, which copies the Java helper's
  topic/body/flag/property values and leaves the transaction ID unset. Producer
  selector preparation now uses the same method. Rust-owned snapshots have
  independent body/property storage; the pinned Java helper shares those
  references.
- Added a direct Java `messagePublicApi` invocation and Rust differential for
  the helper's field projection, distinct result, transaction-ID omission, and
  source retention. Updated the Phase 8 method matrix and release checklist.
  Message fixture SHA-256:
  `7c61fee7311b7926b92b845899083e5f80a2ba8e67105ed7656de3d5e3a17a22`.
- Fixture generation initially ran Maven's existing compiled class and left the
  JSON stale; the first Rust differential then failed because the new fixture
  keys were absent. Recompiled the Java harness with `mvn compile exec:java`,
  regenerated the fixture, and reran the differential successfully.
- Validation: Common `message_public_api_matches_java_551_fixture` PASS;
  Producer `invoke_message_queue_selector_returns_the_namespaced_queue_without_sending`
  PASS; strict all-target/all-feature Clippy for Common and Producer PASS;
  `TZ=Asia/Taipei mvn -q -o -f compat/java-reference/pom.xml verify` PASS
  (37 scenarios, fixture drift checks, and Java/Rust cross-decodes); workspace
  formatting and `git diff --check` PASS.
- This closes the direct `cloneMessage` method mapping only. Broad P18-V01,
  current-revision full P18-V02, GitHub Ubuntu address-profile evidence, Phase
  19 Broker/Docker automation, and release version/registry checks remain open.
- P18-V01/P18-V02 follow-up: the workspace UTC run exposed that Java's
  `getNearlyTimeFromID` fixture stored an absolute epoch tied to the fixture
  generation month and timezone. Replaced it with the Java result's delta from
  its selected local month start, which is stable across month rollovers and
  zones; updated the differential and Producer matrix. Fixture SHA-256:
  `0e63b403150e979b8d10baae980fcd5283343f9092f63308b9bbed95f250c8b6`.
- Added an explicit CI run of the near-time differential under
  `TZ=Asia/Taipei`; the default workspace CI continues to run under Ubuntu UTC.
  Focused Core tests pass under both UTC and Asia/Taipei, and the regenerated
  Java Producer fixture verifies under UTC. Full P18-V02 must be rerun after
  this follow-up commit.
- P18-V02 server-free verification on current revision `1aae4772` (2026-10-15):
  `TZ=UTC cargo test --workspace --locked` and
  `cargo test --workspace --all-features --locked` pass. Strict workspace
  Clippy, `mvn -q -f compat/java-reference/pom.xml verify` (37 scenarios,
  fixture drift and Java/Rust cross-decodes), strict
  `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features --locked -- -D warnings`,
  comparator self-test and
  37-scenario manifest validation, `bash tests/stress/run-offline-smoke.sh`
  (16 cases × 3), fuzz smoke (104 frame seeds, 10 message seeds, 1,824
  mutations), release example build, workspace benchmark compilation, locked
  Cargo metadata, workspace metadata/license/dependency checks, seven package
  content listings, formatting and `git diff --check` pass. The near-time
  ClientID differential passes under UTC and Asia/Taipei. This closes only the
  current revision's server-free P18-V02 gate; P18-V01, current-revision GitHub
  Ubuntu address-profile evidence, Phase 19 Broker/Docker validation, and
  release version/registry checks remain open.
- P18-V01 Java oracle for nullable reserved-property-set membership:
  against pinned RocketMQ 5.5.1, `MessageConst.STRING_HASH_SET` accepts null;
  while null is present, `Message.putUserProperty(null, "value")` throws the
  base `java.lang.RuntimeException` before blank-name validation. Added the
  invoked fixture case and regenerated `fixtures/messages/records.json` with
  `mvn -q -f compat/java-reference/pom.xml compile exec:java
  -Dexec.args='message-decode-fixtures fixtures/messages/records.json false'`;
  the focused Java fixture verification passes. Fixture SHA-256:
  `80f920015068610174b266111497c018abf9ca4c8b183d6233471a81772f0723`.
  Rust behavior is not yet updated; that parity change and differential remain
  open.
- P18-V01 oracle refinement: the same mutable Java set also accepts an empty
  name. With `""` present, `Message.putUserProperty("", "value")` throws the
  base `java.lang.RuntimeException` before blank-name validation. Regenerated
  and verified the Java message fixture; current SHA-256:
  `cd48ccada3c107facb4ec332316ef29e569cca7c50cd3b0711152b7234cd6b98`.
